Read the verdict's places from a point no hidden part can move. In Sampling.ranked, replace `local ox, oz = gripPlace(parts, gripSlot, nil)` with `local ox, oz = outlinePlace(parts)`. outlinePlace loops over every part with p.volume >= Geo.MIN_PART_VOLUME, takes lox/hix = min/max of p.minx/p.maxx and loz/hiz likewise, and returns (lox + hix) / 2, (loz + hiz) / 2, or 0, 0 when there is no such part. It keeps §4.1's rules. Exact code: shift-v2-1/out/repair_vby_src.diff. Tried in var/vby, together with the height fix below:
- the speck case reads 0.2167 Hard in all 9 cases;
- my hidden block on every valid fixture moves nothing (on live it moves X01, X01raw and X02);
- all 33,389 plausible designs, the 136 fixtures, the 200 generated designs and DEADBEEF's 500 read to the bit as live, and so do the X and Z images of the fixtures and generated designs and the id shuffles;
- --quick: 718 pass, 0 fail.
Two test changes go with it (out/repair_vby_tests.diff). First, Verdict.spec's Sampling.ranked case needs a frame part, H.solid(9, 'Block', { 0, 0.5, 0 }, H.I, { 0.2, 0.2, 0.6 }), so that the box is centred on z = 0; its rows become { 9, 1, 2 }, { 9, 1, 2 } and { 9, 2, 1 }. Second, a new pin: P5 with its grip copied 4e-9 along X plus the speck gives the same kept flags and steps. It passes on vby and fails on live ('kept 2') and on the height-only repair. The SPEC's §4.4 ranks paragraph should then read 'its place across from the centre of the box of every part but Dust', and the hidden-Grip remainder goes from §4.4, §5's promise, §5.6, O11 (j) and §17.2. Not measured: an Enclosed part that pokes past the outline within the 2 % rule can still widen the box.
